<<~ ahu #head >>

! New Delos Nexus ~ Region Worksheet

''Four strata, one vertical Nexus.'' An Aegean low-sea archipelago of the Eastern Net — rocky
coastlines, olive-grove terraces, volcanic islands, crystal-clear harbors — with a flying capital
suspended over a megadungeon mouth, and beneath the mouth, the deep dark. Dream-mirror source:
Delos and Thira in an Ice Age low-sea period, pre-Hellenic sacred geographies overlaid.

''Timeline spine:'' YOLD 5002 — the Patroness stabilizes the Nexus, forces the arguing seas back
to the Apophis Datum, and ''levitates the holy sites and most-populated neighborhoods whole'' —
cellars, bones, and smuggler-works included; the craters left below expose the megadungeon mouth.
The same year she transmits the ''Declaration of Confederation'', founding the League of Free
Cities. Mana lifts near the major Lares landmarks join the strata.

This worksheet grows by play; each stratum carries prompts beside its canon.

<<~/ahu >>

<<~ ahu #high-delos >>

!! High Delos ~ the flying capital

''Canon:'' the Lindwyrm's capital and seat of the League of Free Cities. Cycladic marble footings
under Neo-Thracian brick under fae-grown coral — polyglot architecture on Delian designs, arched
walkways between raised neighborhoods, one bridge trussed with a repurposed trireme keel. The
levitated ''Theatre Quarter'' holds the wealthiest old houses, ''the House of Masks'' among them
(cabaret, maze-Inn, Order of Amaranth management — its own loci carry it). The ''Terrace of the
Lions'' gazes over open cloud; the round ''Sacred Lake'' rides the island; the ''Orrery of High
Delos'' turns somewhere near the summit of civic pride. The ''High Delos Archive'' seats the
Floating Librarians of Mu. Archive- and Market-Lares dominate the node traffic.

''Prompts:'' which neighborhoods rose and which stayed? Who regulates the lift-queues? Where does
the Orrery actually sit, and who reads it?

<<~/ahu >>

<<~ ahu #low-delos >>

!! Low Delos ~ the megadungeon mouth

''Canon:'' the craters beneath the flying city expose a megadungeon ''piercing deep into the
Underdark, with stabilized towns down to the third level''. The crater-glow brightens and dims on
a nineteen-minute cycle that correlates with nothing and has outlasted four scholarly careers.
Scavenger-tier salvage economy; a "soulbound lash" of Rakshasa's anger came up from here.
Path-Lares maintain active Underdark maps. Mana lifts run between the ports of High and Low.

''Prompts:'' what do the three stabilized town-levels each trade? Who holds the lift-gates at the
bottom? What does the nineteen-minute cycle breathe FOR?

<<~/ahu >>

<<~ ahu #underdark >>

!! The Underdark ~ below the lowest layer

''Canon:'' Low Delos ranks among ''the deepest, most stable Nexus-to-Underdark routes'' in the
known world — a strategic fact the League guards. Underdark incursions number among the Nexus's
standing hazards; relic-hunting mercenaries destabilize dungeon floors. Past the stabilized
levels, the layers stop pretending to be layers.

''Prompts:'' which deep polities trade and which raid? What does the Menzoberranzan-shaped hole
in Rhea's past imply about routes from HERE? Where do the whispered House-of-Masks ways come out?

<<~/ahu >>

<<~ ahu #outer-seas >>

!! The Outer Seas, Islands & Shores

''Canon:'' surrounding ports and fishing towns scatter across the nearby islands, each with its
own trade goods and Lares shrines. Wave-jammers skim the crystal harbors; the Astral Sea gnaws
the coastlines; contested Astral waters carry diplomatic traffic and smuggling wars both.
Political intrigue among the Free Cities rides every tide-table. The volcanic Thira-mirror
islands stand in the chain; the flotilla-fresco regatta tradition dresses festival days.

''Prompts:'' name five ports and their one export each. Which island keeps the oldest
First-Breaking cult fragment? Where do the smuggling wars actually land their cargo?

<<~/ahu >>

